642 0 obj
<<
/Title (Nitration of isatoic anhydride 4 yields nitro 5 \(Scheme 1\). Methanolysis of anhydride 5 yielded amino-ester 6. By rea-  -cting compound 6 with 2, 5-dimethoxy tetrahydrofu ran in acetic acid, amino functionality was changed to pyrrole ring \(7\). Vilsmeyer Hack formylation of chemical 7 produced aldehyde 8, which was reduced with sodium borohydride and acidified to benz-azulene molecule 9. Compound 11 was formed via nitro to amine and CBzCl protection of amine, which was treated with \(R\)-glycidyl butyrate in BuLi to yield alcohol 12. Mesylation and sodium azide displacement transformed 12's alcohol functionality to azide 13.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 572 0 R
>>
endobj
643 0 obj
